docs={"PROJECT.md":"# Roblox game — shared project brief\n\n## Identity and working location\n\n- Studio place: **money**, ID **94130990350526**.\n- Canonical folder: **C:\\Users\\wikto\\Desktop\\Roblox Gra**. The Documents ca folder is historical.\n- The actual game lives in Studio. Local files are a source mirror, notes, builders and selected assets; they are **not a complete place export**.\n- Read the current handoff at the top of STATUS.md, then only the sources relevant to the task. Verify the connected place and current scripts before editing. Chat histories and uploaded project files do not synchronize automatically.\n\n## Accepted direction\n\nA bright, cartoony snow-digging/RNG simulator for kids and teens: roll shovels, dig Snow, buy upgrades, collect pets and treasures, unlock biomes and rebirth. Keep progression varied, with readable silhouettes, colorful landmarks and playful feedback.\n\n- **Latest pacing target (2026-10-02):** fast start, slower later; World 1, ending at the Absolute Zero Portal, should take **more than 3 hours without paid boosts**. Claude's latest model includes events, daily rewards, quests and achievements: about 4 hours for an efficient engaged solo player, about 5 hours casual, about 6 hours ignoring rewards. These are model estimates, not measured human playthroughs.\n- Art: simple attractive, chunky rounded 3D models; snowy ground, icy blue shadows, warm hut lighting. User requested Blender scenery across all eight World 1 stages. The AllStages pack remains prepared; consult STATUS.md before importing or replacing scenery.\n- **Frostfall Village is the approved active lobby.** Preserve the archived original in ServerStorage.OldLobbyBackup.\n- Only the floating egg/chances panel should have a transparent outer background. Preserve other GUI unless requested.\n- The earlier egg redesign was rejected. Seven later Blender biome eggs form the current hatchable lobby display; do not reinstall rejected designs.\n- User wants requested work implemented in the game, unless they explicitly request only a prompt.\n- Preserve unrelated work, ownership IDs, player progress, and recoverable replacements. Do not publish or reset real player data without explicit instruction.\n\n## Current systems — verified from Studio on 2026-10-02\n\n| Area | Current behavior and source |\n|---|---|\n| World 1 balance | Stage costs: Desert 2.5K, Cursed 250K, Crystal 54M, Retro 4B, Jungle 135B, Absolute Zero 2.5T, Portal 150T Snow. Stage eggs, rebirth milestones and stage-locked upgrades were scaled with the balance pass. StageConfig / PetConfig / RebirthConfig / UpgradeConfig. |\n| Upgrades | **110 tiles**, across Snow, Rolls and Misc. Explicit costs/stage locks; IDs preserve purchases. Luck tiles add percentages; shovels contribute neutral x1 luck. Balance.PowerExponent=0.63. Golden Dice starts every 10 rolls, improves to 5 (x3 luck); Rainbow starts every 100, improves to 50 (x10). |\n| Rebirth | +0.50 Snow and +0.25 luck per rebirth, additive, cap 50. Resets Snow/stages/upgrades while retaining pets, shovels and discoveries. First milestone: Cursed + 62K Snow. RebirthConfig / RebirthService / RebirthRules. |\n| Pets and eggs | **7 hatchable eggs, 35 pets**, including Retro/Jungle/AbsoluteZero. PetConfig / PetModels / PetService / StarterGui.RNGGui.PetClient. FrostfallVillage.EggDisplay contains the world eggs; EggFloat animates them. PetClient shows nearest odds and clones the Shell for hatching. |\n| Shovel mutations | Giant: 1 in 5, x2 size/reach. Shiny: 1 in 10, x3 power. Shiny Giant combines them. RNGConfig / RNGHandler / ShovelOrbit / SnowFieldService. Index has Normal/Giant/Shiny/Shiny Giant tabs. |\n| Snow fields | Workspace.SnowFieldZones defines Edit-time boxes; SnowFieldData and tiles are built during Play. SnowFields / SnowFieldService / SnowFieldClient. Sakura has its own template and two zones. |\n| Buried Treasures | Fully dug tiles roll 1/100; first treasure guaranteed on the third tile. 7 biome sets, 5 rarities, 35 collection items; average Snow bonus about 6% of digging income. Collection survives rebirth. **36 PNG slots are populated** (35 treasures + menu chest). TreasureConfig / TreasureIcon / TreasureModels chest fallback / TreasureService / TreasureBook / TreasureReveal. Luck does not change these odds. Art: outputs/TreasureIcons20261001/generated-20261002/. |\n| Rewards / Activities | New REWARDS left-menu button and panel with Daily, Quests, Achievements and Codes. 7-day rewards, 3 quests with a 30-minute refresh after all claims, **19 permanent-bonus achievements**, server events Snowstorm/Lucky Wind/Aurora about every 10–15 minutes. ActivityConfig / ActivityService / BoostService / ActivityClient. Codes live server-side in ActivityService. Profile fields d.Activity and d.SnowEarned; UpgradeService applies Snow/luck boosts. |\n| World 2 | Sakura Garden, stage 9, opens automatically with Portal. Workspace.World2 is the 260 x 100 strip at x1565..1825, z−50..50; two 120 x 30 fields, cherry trees, lanterns, pagoda, pond/bridge, torii return portal. StageService streams and teleports; respawning in World 2 returns to its plaza. Sakura lighting profile is installed. Blender templates: ServerStorage.World2PropTemplates. Candy Kingdom is only a coming-soon gate. |\n| Intro / starter shovel | About 7.9-second lobby storyboard: sky fall, landing, shovel discovery/grab, two-handed victory, close-up, gameplay handoff. Existing **Tin Shovel**, the least rare base shovel; StarterShovelRules grants it once per eligible profile and preserves better equipment. SnowIntroController / SnowIntroRig / SnowIntroArt / SnowIntroService / SnowIntro bootstrap. Skip and Studio I replay retained. ReplicatedFirst.LoadingScreen covers joining. |\n| Tutorial / lobby | TutorialClient: roll, collect 10 Snow, open upgrades; prefers FrostfallSnowYard. Lobby origin (−105, 0.24, −282), spawn near (−167, 0.32, −282). FrostfallClient / FrostfallTravel / VillageOpenMenu. Cabins have repaired rear gables; paths join; snow globe uses existing Gold and Absolute Zero shovel models. |\n| Upgrade UI | **UpgradeTreeClient v3**: Snow/Rolls share the main branch, Misc link/back switches pages. Owned + attached frontier + mystery ring; one-tap buying, green affordable/red unaffordable/blue owned. Larger PNG icons; preserves UpgradeTreeGui name for tutorial. Studio-only. |\n| Sound | RollController has crisp prize-wheel ticks, speed-based pitch, landing click, quieter mini mode. RNGGui attributes RollTickVolume / RollTickOff control them. Studio-only; consult sound handoffs before changing asset IDs. |\n| Lighting / scenery | ReplicatedFirst.BiomeLighting + Profiles grade areas, including Sakura; Lighting.BiomeGrade. FrostfallLobbyDecor / CursedStageDecor / StageDecor20260930 contain current scenery. StageDecorClient animates nearby bob/Water/Sway/Orbit/Roll props and culls distant particles. Earlier scene counts are historical; inspect current objects. |\n\n## Source mirroring, Rojo and Graphify\n\nThe 2026-10-02 refresh captured current Edit sources: **45 scripts in game/src** for ReplicatedStorage, ServerScriptService and StarterPlayerScripts, plus **23 read-only scripts in game/studio-snapshots** for StarterGui, ReplicatedFirst, Workspace and active ServerStorage helpers. Two generic Workspace.Script copies are archive-only. The source manifest records actual classes, RunContext, paths and hashes.\n\n- default.project.json maps only ReplicatedStorage, ServerScriptService and StarterPlayerScripts. StarterGui, Workspace, ServerStorage and ReplicatedFirst remain Studio-managed.\n- A Workspace Script may use RunContext=Client; check the snapshot manifest rather than inferring execution from its filename.\n- The SnowStages folder now preserves unknown Studio children so an unmapped Sakura template is retained. Existing stage economic attributes matched disk.\n- Existing binary .rbxm models were not re-exported or verified. Sakura geometry/template, GUI hierarchy, lighting instances and map models remain in Studio. This folder cannot rebuild the full place.\n- No active Rojo server/plugin connection was verified during this refresh. Before connecting, verify the server serves this canonical folder and review its proposed changes. Never connect the historical ca/game server or let old disk sources overwrite newer Studio work.\n- **Laptop Claude chat:** its uploaded files are static copies. After a refresh, re-upload the latest PROJECT.md, STATUS.md, graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md and graph.json, or use the handoff ZIP. No automatic memory sharing.\n- Graphify scans game/ only. For code questions, query the scoped graph first; then verify live sources. Refresh snapshots after Studio edits, then run Refresh-Graph.ps1. A disk-only rebuild cannot capture live changes.\n- Latest graph: **530 nodes, 1,027 edges, 42 communities**. Extraction warned about partial parsing in UpgradeTreeClient and PortalAnimator around Luau compound assignments. Graphify is navigation aid, not a Roblox compiler or runtime test.\n\n## Tests, recovery and current limits\n\nPrefer Studio tools for live changes and re-read affected sources before applying prepared patches because Claude and Codex can share the place. Workspace contains duplicate names; a dot path may be ambiguous.\n\nFor isolated progression tests, set ServerStorage.BalanceTestMode=true in **Edit before Play**, stop only your own Play session afterward, and remove the attribute in Edit. It isolates the main DataService, not every third-party system. Direct MCP module requires/test hooks can be blocked by Studio command capabilities; do not weaken those capabilities.\n\nLatest recovery/export evidence: outputs/StudioRefresh20261002/ (live source archive, per-source hashes, before copies and sync report). Claude balance backups: ServerStorage.BalanceBackups.Before_20261002_FastStart / Before_20261002_Activities / Before_20261002_Balance_v2. Older art, lobby and intro backups remain recoverable; never blindly rerun historical builders.\n\nOpen issues and the next checks are at the top of STATUS.md. Implemented, tested, saved and published states must be stated separately.\n","game/studio-snapshots/README.md":"# Studio-only source snapshots\n\nCaptured from **money (94130990350526), Edit, 2026-10-02**. These 23 scripts are read-only reference copies for Graphify and are outside default.project.json mappings.\n\nIncluded: 13 StarterGui.RNGGui scripts/modules, ReplicatedFirst loading/biome lighting plus Profiles, Workspace portal/egg/palette scripts, and four active ServerStorage helpers (AdminConfig, AdminConsole.ConsoleClient, ShovelModelBuilder, older SnowFields helper).\n\nEdit the actual Studio source, then refresh its snapshot. Editing one of these files does not install it into Studio. Paths, actual ClassName, Disabled, RunContext and SHA-256 are recorded in ../../outputs/StudioRefresh20261002/sync-report.json. PortalAnimator and EggFloat are **Scripts with RunContext=Client** despite the .server.luau filenames, which reflect their ClassName. Two duplicate generic Workspace.Script sources are archive-only.\n\nlive-instance-summary.json records current remote classes, SnowStages attributes, field names, Rewards presence, backups and World 2 facts. It is not a serialized place, GUI or mesh export.\n\nOld flattened UpgradeTreeClient and misclassified EggFloat snapshots, plus the unmapped game/src/ReplicatedFirst/LoadingScreen copy, were archived before consolidating them here. Existing binary models were not changed.\n\nGraphify refresh: 530 nodes / 1,027 edges / 42 communities. UpgradeTreeClient and PortalAnimator produced partial AST warnings near compound assignments; consult their live sources for full context. No Play, save, persistence or publishing test was performed by this source refresh.\n","game/README.txt":"Source mirror for Roblox Studio \"money\" (94130990350526)\nCanonical folder: C:\\Users\\wikto\\Desktop\\Roblox Gra\\game\n\ndefault.project.json maps ONLY:\n  src/ReplicatedStorage\n  src/ServerScriptService\n  src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts\n\nStarterGui, ReplicatedFirst, Workspace and ServerStorage are Studio-managed.\nRead-only script references for those services are in studio-snapshots/.\nThe refresh of 2026-10-02 verified 68 source copies against live Edit.\nThis is NOT a complete exported game. Existing binary models were not refreshed.\nSnowStages/init.meta.json preserves unknown Studio children, including Sakura.\n\nsyncback.project.json is an auxiliary export configuration; it is not proof\nof two-way sync or a live connection. It maps the same three service roots.\n\nBefore rojo serve, verify the canonical folder, current Studio sources and\nthe plugin's proposed changes. Do not run the historical Documents ca/game copy.\nNo Rojo connection was verified by the latest refresh.\n\nRefresh graph only after current Studio sources have reached these files:\n  project-root\\Refresh-Graph.ps1\n\nLatest notes: project-root\\PROJECT.md and STATUS.md.\nRecovery/evidence: outputs\\StudioRefresh20261002.\n","PROJECT-INSTRUCTIONS.txt":"You are helping build my bright, cartoony Roblox snow-digging/RNG simulator, Studio place \"money\" (94130990350526).\n\nAt the start of a chat, read AGENTS.md, PROJECT.md and the CURRENT HANDOFF at the top of STATUS.md. Then inspect only the sources relevant to the request. Do not reread every chat or backup. If files are inaccessible or only uploaded copies are available, say so; never pretend they are live.\n\nCanonical folder: C:\\Users\\wikto\\Desktop\\Roblox Gra. The actual game lives in Roblox Studio. Verify the connected place and current sources before editing; another assistant may have newer changes. The Documents ca folder is historical.\n\nLatest pacing target: fast start, slower later; World 1 (ending at the Absolute Zero Portal) >3 hours without paid boosts. Latest model includes events, daily rewards, quests and achievements: about 4 hours efficient engaged, 5 hours casual. These are estimates, not a human playthrough. Preserve the current server-validated economy and ownership IDs.\n\nFrostfall Village is the approved active lobby; preserve the archived original. Only the egg/chances panel should have a transparent outer background. Keep the current later Blender eggs; the original rejected designs must not return. Respect the user's latest request, including prompt-only requests.\n\nImplement authorized work directly when tools are available. Keep explanations short, make routine reversible choices without repeated confirmation, preserve unrelated work and recoverable replacements. Never publish or reset real player data without explicit instruction.\n\nGraphify: use graphify query for relevant code when the CLI is available; otherwise navigate the latest uploaded graph.json / GRAPH_REPORT.md and verify the live scripts. The graph indexes game/src plus read-only game/studio-snapshots for UI, lighting, Workspace and active ServerStorage helpers. Snapshots are not writable live sources. Refresh Studio→disk first, then run Refresh-Graph.ps1. The graph does not describe binary meshes or prove runtime behavior.\n\nRojo maps ReplicatedStorage, ServerScriptService and StarterPlayerScripts only. GUI, ReplicatedFirst, Workspace and ServerStorage are Studio-managed. Do not connect stale disk sources or the old ca/game server. Claude on a laptop without folder access uses live Studio tools; uploaded notes/maps do not update automatically.\n\nFor an isolated progression Play test, set ServerStorage.BalanceTestMode=true in Edit first. Stop your own Play session and remove the flag afterward; it protects only the main DataService. Do not stop another person's Play or bypass command capabilities.\n\nAfter meaningful work, update STATUS.md with implemented changes, evidence, unresolved issues and next action; update PROJECT.md for lasting decisions. Distinguish implemented, tested, saved and published. With uploaded-only context, return a replacement STATUS.md for the shared folder.\n"}
